[32m✔ frame interpolation pricing context normalizes resolution and fps tiers [90m(5.6939ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ frame interpolation submit uses the official client_token field [90m(3529.873ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ frame interpolation persists provider identity, local output, exact settlement, and idempotent replay [90m(6013.1065ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ completed-video output never falls back to a supplier signed URL [90m(8.0515ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ video list exposes a durable local poster path without mounting video bytes [90m(137.7635ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ homepage defaults use the configured product media resources rather than any user videos [90m(56.8149ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ a completed local video remains completed when OSS archival is temporarily unavailable [90m(54.2028ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ startup reconciliation invalidates historical completed rows without a local archive [90m(10.5954ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ video post-processing defaults to preserving the generated source [90m(22.0512ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ 480p supports optional 720p or 1080p enhancement [90m(2.0151ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ 720p supports only an optional 1080p enhancement [90m(5.09ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ 1080p cannot be redundantly enhanced and 2K is not an exposed target [90m(2.5957ms)[39m[39m
[32m✔ interpolation is independent from enhancement and may be disabled [90m(1.8202ms)[39m[39m
